Faciolock greeters for Plasma and SDDM
======================================

The package selects the Faciolock Breeze SDDM theme and diverts only Plasma's
LockScreen.qml entry file. Plasma's original entry is retained as
FaciolockStockLockScreen.qml, so the standard lock-screen layout, password
field, session controls and power controls remain in use. Removing the package
restores the original entry and the previous SDDM theme selection.

Automatic scanning requires an enrolled face and an enabled PAM profile. The
Plasma lock-screen process also needs access to the faciolock-auth socket group;
log out and back in after group membership changes. The password prompt remains
available if the face check cannot complete.

Use the System Settings Face Unlock switch or `sudo faciolockctl enable` and
`sudo faciolockctl disable` to change the global setting. These commands keep
the greeter setting at /etc/xdg/faciolock-greeter.conf in sync with PAM. Direct
changes through pam-auth-update require a matching enable/disable command to
refresh the greeter setting.

SDDM reports when a login attempt begins and ends, rather than the exact moment
the camera stops. Its scanning indicator ends on a login result or after seven
seconds. The daemon limits camera capture separately to six seconds.

 -- Faciolock contributors
